ok heres the practise I want to carry out in daily life.

at the moment I am having nibbana moments

which are basically when it is pure seeing without a seer

the dropping away of the movie, plot and actor

these moments appear to be uncaused, yet I can engineer the conditions for when they are likely to arise

e.g. they are impossible to happen if I am watching youtube

if i am scrolling twitter

if i am absorbed in any thing

becuase then there is no possibility of attention to rest on itself

which is waht it feels like 

i cant really describe the experience, or make it happen if i tried

even thinking back to these moments i cant re-expeirence them

it can only be seen right now


it is also pointless to just sit here and force myself to see it right now continuosly

tomorrow I wake up and forget what i am trying to do, what i have seen and whats really going on

my practise is throughout the day to leave myself mental checkpoints when these experiences happen

and just generally throughout the day so that in the evening when I replay my day I can latch onto them as stable points of reference

the overall goal being, I can recall teh events of the day

then recall these nirvana moments and use them as triggers to see nirvana right now

the goal is to hack the attainment of nibbana

seems to be simple. in any situation you are faced with a choice, favour letting go 

e.g. do you want sugar, no

do you want a cigarette, no

shall i buy this thing, no

shall i scroll for a bit, no

the intention is to always, to pull the mind out from its repeated habits of absorption it is currently being pulled into as a way of regulating

when a mechanical action occurs, what uncomfortable things is beeing sootehd by this behaviour

piercing that uncomfortable thing is the practise

and you only get the opportunity when you catch yourself in that absorption phase

you find yourself openning twitter, thats the moment, become intensely aware right then

like a fire, you see with clarity you didnt choose to open twitter, in that moment the mechanism of craving is seen as pure habit

not resting on any other thing, occuring completely without basis, an action not chosen by you

yet one that pulls you are traps you

this is the dangerous trap that you do not realise you are in

that sounds crazy until you see it

but its actually unbelievable and revolutionary

yet seeing it will actaully make you appear crazy

because the world finds comfort in delusion

and calling the ones who see truth delusional

because evolution does not optimise for truth, preferring survival

so to see truth is to go against the appearance of reality to some degree

how reality appears to me is an itnerface optimised for survival and social well being

how it actually is, is far more horrific and beautiful

there is only seeing, action without an owner














